  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Web Service**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on defining the web service\'s core purpose, guided by the user\'s specific requests. The emphasis is firmly on UI/UX, especially concerning \"resume assistance\" and \"portfolio assistance\" features. My focus remains on features to be available to support the user.\n\n\n**Visualizing the React App**\n\nI\'m solidifying the architecture: a single-page React app with Tailwind CSS and all content in Korean. I\'ve begun analyzing the provided screenshots and the design elements they represent. The structure of the application is clearly beginning to take form. I\'m focusing on user interface elements.\n\n\n**Refining the UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now concretizing the visual language of the application. I\'m focusing on color choices, typography scales, grid-based layouts, and shadow styles for UI elements. I\'ve noted that I\'ll use soft, professional shadows and a base radius of 8px. I\'ve made adjustments regarding gradients, ensuring a flat, clean design. I must also add loading states for all async operations.\n\n\n**Outlining the App Structure**\n\nI\'m now outlining the `App.tsx` file. I\'ll use state to manage different views (landing, dashboard, resume, portfolio) within the single file constraint. I\'m focusing on components, particularly shared elements like `TopNav` (with view-specific variations) and `SideNav` (for the dashboard). I\'ll also create view components like `LandingView` and `DashboardView` to handle their respective content. Icons will be imported from `lucide-react`, mapping from the provided visual references.\n\n\n**Structuring the Views**\n\nI\'m now focusing on specific views. `ResumeEditorView` will be split into a top bar, editor, and AI sidebar. `PortfolioBuilderView` will have a top bar, element panel, canvas, and styles panel. The main `App` component now manages the `currentView` state.\n\nI\'m also setting design guidelines: no gradients, using a soft shadow, and implementing specific hex codes if Tailwind defaults don\'t suffice. I\'m focusing on consistency across the app.\n\n\n**Defining Style Principles**\n\nI\'m now focusing on background and border colors, establishing the foundation of the app\'s visual identity. I\'m noting specific hex codes: `#F8FAFC` for backgrounds (matching slate-50) and `#E2E8F0` for borders (corresponding to slate-200). These will be critical when Tailwind defaults are insufficient. I\'m focusing on defining UI visual elements.\n\n\n**Constructing the Components**\n\nNow, I\'m diving into coding the `PortfolioBuilderView`. I\'ve outlined the three-column layout, including the browser-like canvas for content display and the top bar with preview and publish functions. My focus now is on implementing navigation, specifically linking buttons and links to ensure a smooth transition from the landing page to the dashboard, and then to the resume/portfolio sections. I\'m also mapping icons to the `lucide-react` library.\n\n\n**Mapping Icon Equivalents**\n\nI\'ve completed mapping the provided icon descriptions to their corresponding `lucide-react` equivalents. I\'ve also defined the state management for view switching within the React app. I\'ve confirmed that the core application state is set, in order to allow for view navigation and management.\n\n\n\n**Defining Color Variables**\n\nI\'m now establishing specific color values for Tailwind customization: primary text and background are `#002045`. I\'ll use `#38A169` for success backgrounds, white for surfaces, and `#F8FAFC` and `#E2E8F0` for backgrounds and borders. I\'ll implement a subtle shadow: `shadow-[0_4px_6px_-1px_rgba(26,54,93,0.05),0_2px_4px_-1px_rgba(26,54,93,0.03)]`. I\'m focusing on defining color-related variables.\n\n\\n\\n\n\nI\'ve replaced a gradient in the \"Career Analysis\" bento grid item with the primary color, ensuring white text for contrast. I am also implementing \"loading states\" for UI responsiveness, using an `isLoading` state variable to simulate async delays for transitions between different views.\n\n\n**Coding the React App**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `App.tsx` file, starting with import statements, type definitions, and the `LoadingOverlay` component. I\'m focusing on creating the core components (`Landing`, `Dashboard`, `ResumeEditor`, `PortfolioBuilder`) and integrating them into the main app. I\'ve confirmed that Korean text and single-file structure constraints are met, along with the lack of gradients and simulated loading states. I\'m focusing on the component implementation, and confirming UI/UX goals are implemented.\n\n\n"
