  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Redesigning the App**\n\nI\'m focused on the redesign, given the new product requirements document. My current effort is centered around incorporating the \"AI Career Copilot\" concept into the application, specifically the four key pillars: Candidate Vault, 3C4P Experience Decomposer, JD Analyzer, and Strategy modules. I\'m exploring the best way to integrate these functionalities seamlessly.\n\n\n**Visualizing the Application Pipeline**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the application pipeline visualization. The revised dashboard concept involves an asset vault and a new application pipeline, instead of standard project lists. I\'ve broken this down into asset upload, JD analysis/matching, strategy formulation, document generation/verification, and a defense test phase. My thinking is to create a new `PipelineView` or modify the `DashboardView` to reflect this flow. I\'m also planning updates to the `ResumeEditorView` to feature \"Evidence View\" and the \"Defense Test\" concepts. I\'ll need to refactor `App.tsx`, changing the `ViewState` to reflect a pipeline-centered dashboard and updating `LandingView` to emphasize \"Evidence-based AI\".\n\n\n**Refining the UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the individual views. I\'m modifying `DashboardView` to prominently feature the \"Candidate Vault\" and application pipeline, while also refactoring `ResumeEditorView` to incorporate evidence checks (with visual cues like warning and check marks) and the \"Defense Test\" sidebar. The `PortfolioBuilderView` might be retained, but the messaging will be tweaked to emphasize JD strategy integration.\n\n\n**Implementing the Changes**\n\nI\'m now fully focused on implementing the structural changes in `App.tsx`. Given the extent of the refactor and the file\'s size, I\'ve decided to overwrite the entire file with a fresh, pipeline-centric structure using `default_api:create_file` with `Overwrite: true`. I\'ve also incorporated the necessary lucide-react icons, including `Database`, `Target`, `ShieldCheck`, `CheckSquare`, and `AlertTriangle`, and defined the new file structure.\n\n\n**Updating the Editor View**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the `EditorView`. I plan to simplify the views to \'landing\', \'dashboard\', and \'editor\'. The editor will have a left side for the document, with highlighted sentences and icons to show AI analysis, and a right sidebar for the AI assistant. The sidebar will feature tabs for \"\354\247\200\354\233\220 \354\240\204\353\236\265\" (Strategy), \"\354\210\253\354\236\220/\352\267\274\352\261\260 \352\262\200\354\246\235\" (Evidence), and \"\353\251\264\354\240\221 \353\260\251\354\226\264\" (Defense), with the \"Defense\" tab providing an interactive chat for practice.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
