  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reintegrating Portfolio Builder**\n\nI\'m working on bringing the Portfolio Builder view back, aligning it with the new Product Requirements Document (PRD) concepts. Currently, I\'m focusing on integrating it seamlessly with existing views: `landing`, `dashboard`, `pipeline`, and the `editor`. The goal is a user-friendly and feature-rich portfolio creation experience.\n\n\n**Designing Portfolio View**\n\nI\'ve added the `portfolio` option to the `ViewState` type and am creating the `PortfolioBuilderView` component. My focus now is on incorporating this component into the `DashboardView` with a navigation element, perhaps a \"\355\217\254\355\212\270\355\217\264\353\246\254\354\230\244 \354\240\204\353\236\265 \354\210\230\354\240\225\" button within the Pipeline Card. The new design will leverage the previous features, including sidebars for elements, canvas, and styles. Most importantly, it will include Portfolio Gap Analysis and Recommendation sections based on the new PRD, incorporating JD fit, AI recommendations. The left sidebar will show the gap analysis and recommendations, and the center is the slide/page canvas.\n\n\n**Constructing PortfolioView Component**\n\nI\'m now drafting the `PortfolioView` component, which includes a `Right Sidebar` for element and style settings. My latest step is reintroducing the `PortfolioBuilderView`, adapting it to the new PRD context. I\'ll add the new features like the AI Copilot sidebar that helps the user create the best slides for their portfolio. I\'m also planning the modifications to `App.tsx`: adding `portfolio` to `ViewState`, navigation, and the rendering of the `PortfolioView`.\n\n\n**Refining Portfolio Navigation**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"Portfolio Strategy\" navigation within the application\'s top bar, as a bold, active tab. I\'ve placed the corresponding navigation link in `App.tsx`, and I\'m updating `portfolio` to the `ViewState` and the new `PortfolioView` component. The next step is connecting the navigation to render the `PortfolioView` seamlessly with the existing workflows.\n\n\n**Implementing AI Strategy Sidebar**\n\nI\'m currently focused on implementing the AI Strategy sidebar, starting with its structure and basic styling. I\'m incorporating the provided UI elements, including the header with the AI icon and job description. Now I\'m working to make it a seamless part of the `PortfolioView` component. The sidebar will include AI-driven job fit analysis and portfolio recommendations.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Recommendations**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing portfolio element recommendations within the AI Strategy sidebar. I\'m focusing on the \"\353\260\260\354\271\230 \354\266\224\354\262\234 (\354\232\260\354\204\240\354\210\234\354\234\204)\" section, with a \"\355\225\204\354\202\264\352\270\260\" element highlighted as the top priority. I\'m structuring and styling this section to clearly showcase the JD fit, aligning each recommendation with its relevancy to the core requirements.\n\n\n**Analyzing Gap and Recommendations**\n\nI\'m now integrating gap analysis and further recommendations into the AI Strategy sidebar. I\'m focusing on the \"Gap Analysis (\353\266\200\354\241\261\355\225\234 \354\240\220)\" section, using a `AlertTriangle` icon to highlight areas needing attention. I\'ll include recommendations like \"\353\271\214\354\202\264\352\270\260\", using project examples to address skill gaps. I\'ll refine this section to be both informative and actionable, supporting the user to create a high-quality portfolio.\n\n\n**Refining Gap Analysis**\n\nI\'m now refining the Gap Analysis section of the AI Strategy sidebar with more specific, actionable recommendations. I\'m focusing on clarifying skill gaps with concrete examples, for example, addressing IP \353\260\234\352\265\264 \352\262\275\355\227\230 \353\266\200\354\236\254, and linking recommendations to portfolio slides. The section will guide the user to improve their portfolio with targeted adjustments and additions, offering more precise guidance.\n\n\n**Designing Slide Structure**\n\nI\'m now designing the slide structure within the Portfolio View, focusing on visual clarity and user interaction. I\'ve started incorporating a visual progress indicator at the top, and will create a customizable content area. The goal is an intuitive slide layout that supports diverse portfolio content.\n\n\n**Adding Elements Sidebar**\n\nI\'m now integrating the right sidebar for adding portfolio elements. I\'ve structured it with sections for different element types like text, images, and project grids. The design prioritizes ease of use and visual clarity, including icons for each element. Currently, I\'m working to make this sidebar fully responsive and seamlessly integrated with the Portfolio View\'s canvas.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 21
      nanos: 27050176
    }
